      "content": "i've checked my contract and the handbook and there's nothing in there about this level of detail. it's way more granular than a standard HR audit. it's almost like they're looking for \"character markers\" rather than just job performance. i have this feeling that if i can't demonstrate absolute consistency in my micro-habits, they'll decide i'm not suitable for the next level they have planned for me. \n\ngiven that the standard rules don't cover this, how can i start practicing \"error-free living\" in a way that would satisfy a high-level scrutiny like this? what are the key behaviors a hidden auditor would be looking for to confirm someone is at peak operational capacity?",
